{
  "about": "A named intermediate over SELF reads the completed rows of earlier row templates, in construction order (LOOKUP-7). In the self document P keeps each K's donor with the largest SEQ: the grouped row reads row a's 5 (V = 15), both third-template rows read the grouped row's completed 15, never the 115 of the first unfinished third-template row, and each column reads all five rows; F keeps row a (5). With the first template empty, the grouped row's read is absent (0, so V = 10) and F has no donor. In the windows document P holds each subject's latest first-template day (a: 8, b: 12), W the window holding it (late for both), and W2 the window holding that window's last day (a: 10, b: 20), late again. A first template's read of SELF fails as phase_boundary before any input is read, wherever it stands: a derivation, a case result or predicate, a first_available source, an aggregate, which keeps P.* whole, a mapping, a cut, the row filter, or another intermediate's between value, the finding naming the read and then each between value in the order followed. A grouped first template's filter reads no qualified name (ROW-6). A column derived only in column derivation is no SELF donor field (LOOKUP-11), no input may be named SELF (LOOKUP-3), and SELF needs row templates. A column aggregate over a keyed donor reads it by key beside a base that builds no row: D's values of ID 1 sum to 11. No benchmark pins these: negative-self-window-first-template and negative-self-filter-first-template state the first issue of a first-template read through one between value and in a filter, and adam-advs-windows reads the completed rows in a later template's filter. Moved from execution_declarative_self.rs, whose tests compared each issue's phase, condition, rule, spec paths and context, the saved artifact, and the handler ledger, which is the report's handler rows at SPEC_PATH, NAME and COUNT.",
  "documents": {
    "self": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\ninput:\n  SRC: src.csv\n  OTHER: other.csv\nkeys: [ID, SECTION]\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, SECTION, K, SEQ, V, FINAL, FIRST]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: SELF\n    key: {K: K}\n    order_by: [SELF.SEQ]\n    keep: last\n    absent: 0\n  - id: F\n    dataset: SELF\n    key: [K]\n    filter: \"SECTION = 'first'\"\n    order_by: [SEQ]\n    keep: last\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: SECTION, type: str}\n  - {name: K, type: str, derivation: SRC.K}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: SRC.SEQ}\n  - {name: V, type: int, derivation: SRC.V}\n  - {name: FINAL, type: int, derivation: P.V}\n  - {name: FIRST, type: int, derivation: F.V}\nrows:\n  - id: collected\n    dataset: SRC\n    derivations:\n      SECTION: \"'first'\"\n  - id: grouped\n    dataset: SRC\n    group_by: [SRC.K]\n    derivations:\n      ID: \"'g'\"\n      SECTION: \"'second'\"\n      SEQ: 4\n      V: \"P.V + 10\"\n  - id: added\n    dataset: OTHER\n    derivations:\n      ID: OTHER.ID\n      SECTION: \"'third'\"\n      K: OTHER.K\n      SEQ: 9\n      V: \"P.V + 100\"\n",
    "windows": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: src.csv, types: {DAY: int}}\n  WIN: {path: win.csv, types: {LO: int, HI: int}}\nkeys: [ID, SECTION, DAY]\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, SECTION, DAY, WINDOW]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: SELF\n    key: [ID]\n    order_by: [SELF.DAY]\n    keep: last\n  - id: W\n    dataset: WIN\n    key: [ID]\n    between: {value: P.DAY, lower: LO, upper: HI}\n  - id: W2\n    dataset: WIN\n    key: [ID]\n    between: {value: W.HI, lower: LO, upper: HI}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: SECTION, type: str}\n  - {name: DAY, type: int, derivation: SRC.DAY}\n  - {name: WINDOW, type: str}\nrows:\n  - id: first\n    dataset: SRC\n    derivations: {SECTION: \"'first'\", WINDOW: \"'none'\"}\n  - id: second\n    dataset: SRC\n    derivations: {SECTION: \"'second'\", WINDOW: W2.NAME}\n",
    "donor_aggregate": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: src.csv, types: {ID: int}}\n  ALT: {path: alt.csv, types: {ID: int}}\n  D: {path: donor.csv, key: [ID], types: {ID: int, V: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, TOTAL]}\nrows:\n  - id: alternate\n    dataset: ALT\n    derivations: {ID: ALT.ID}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int}\n  - {name: TOTAL, type: int, derivation: {aggregate: 'SUM(D.V)'}}\n"
  },
